#
# Copyright © 2026 Arthur Neto
#
# Made into DEBIAN/control by `make` (see deb.mk), which drops these comments and fills in what's known once the package is staged:
# @VERSION@, @ARCH@, @INSTALLED_SIZE@ (in KiB) and @SHLIBS@ (the packages of the libraries the programs link, found by dpkg-shlibdeps).
#
# The other dependencies are what the programs run but don't link:
# - the EVDI kernel module: evdi-dkms (built for each kernel), or evdi-modules, which the EVDI modules of the Ubuntu kernels provide (signed, for Secure Boot)
# - PipeWire, for the sound
# - pkexec, so polkit asks for the password to create an EVDI device when none is free (e.g. a DisplayLink dock took it)

Package: pspdisp
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Arthur Neto <arthur@net-0.dev>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS@, evdi-dkms | evdi-modules
Recommends: pipewire, pkexec
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/net-0/PSPdisp
Description: Use a PSP as a display of the computer
 PSPdisp turns a PSP into a second display of the computer: the PSP shows a
 virtual display, plays the desktop sound, and its buttons drive a virtual
 gamepad, keyboard or mouse.
 .
 This package has the desktop app (pspdisp-ui) and the daemon that streams to
 the PSP (pspdisp-daemon). The PSP app is installed on the PSP itself.
